# lit = “O you sem-priest, you patrician, you ten great ones of the Palace, you ten great ones of Heliopolis, you Great Ennead, sit down so that you may see the purification of the father of this Pepi with semen and with natron, the spittle which issued from the mouth of Seth, wherewith Horus is purified, wherewith the evil which was on him is cast out on the ground after Seth did against him, wherewith Seth is purified and the evil which was on him is cast out on the ground after Horus did against him, wherewith this Pepi is purified and the evil which was on him is cast out on the ground, being what Nuteknu did against you in company with your spirits.”
# trans = “O you sem-priest, you patrician, you ten great ones of the Palace, you ten great ones of Heliopolis, you Great Ennead, sit down so that the purification of the father of this Pepi with semen and with natron, the spittle which issued from the mouth of Seth, wherewith Horus is purified, wherewith the evil which was on him is cast out on the ground after Seth did against him, wherewith Seth is purified and the evil which was on him is cast out on the ground after Horus did against him, wherewith this Pepi is purified and the evil which was on him is cast out on the ground, being what Nuteknu did against you in company with your spirits.
# type = Verbal sentence with Ellipsis of the apposition
# comment = Sim. Faulkner 1969: 151.
